{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/556317-can-beasts-disable-their-atavisms","id":556317,"title":"Can Beasts disable their Atavisms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-15T18:13:03-07:00","id":556317,"title":"Can Beasts disable their Atavisms?","content":"The Atavisms are all really cool and quite potent, but the way they're described as intrinsic has me wondering if a Beast can ever turn them off? Specifically this is a concern for Limb from Limb, if I have that Atavism am I going to leave crippling injuries even in cases where I want to play with my food, or conceal my nature from the watchful eyes of Hunters and Heroes? I'm just having a difficult time building a Beast that can fight others of his kind but won't annihilate mortals by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:14:48-07:00","id":556330,"title":"","content":"It is still something you have to declare use of, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:10:39-07:00","id":556768,"title":"","content":"From what I understand, Atavisms are turned off by default. I think of it a lot like Majesty in Vampire. You can effectively have it on all the time - no cost, no real mechanical drawback. However, its still decision to choose to have it on, not have it active all the time. There are times when its best to not have it on, though, so you can choose not to activate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:37:50-07:00","id":557011,"title":"","content":"YMMV, of course, but my impression is that the devs intent is for them to be a permanent feature of the character, not an optional thing. I'd generally rule that Atavisms can't be switched off, although you can choose not to make use of their capabilities. Limb From Limb specifically says that you CAN apply the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack tilt, not that you <i>have</i> to. Some of the Atavisms have down-sides for low Satiety that aren't much of a problem if you can just switch it off. I also feel that it makes better thematic sense if you cannot deactivate them entirely, for the same reasons that you don't appear to change when you make use of one.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that a well fed Beast can opt to be gentle/careful but a hungry monster, pacing and agitated in its Lair, doesn't have the patience and control necessary to entirely avoid sticking someone with its claws or shattering bones with a giant fist. &quot;No one walks away from the hungry Beast, not in one piece anyway. The Beast rends flesh by touch alone. His unarmed attacks inflict lethal damage with a weapon modifier equal to his Lair dots.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:54:56-07:00","id":557177,"title":"","content":"I imagine they're always present, but they don't have to be in an active form. An obvious one being the Dragon fire, since I rarely hear stories that involve a dragon having no control over the breath weapon and having to use it on every exhale. Other ones I imagine have kind a minor resonance when you aren't actually drawing on their function. Like Limb from Limb probably functions as you having the kind finger nails that scratch people up or draw blood if you apply too much pressure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:12:00-07:00","id":557232,"title":"","content":"Activisms effects are optional so they only work at the will of the Beast. Limb from Limb in particular requires a reflexive action to use so the Beast would have to turn it on to use it. It is still intrinsic because it can never be suppressed by anyone else. You would need magic to separate the Beast's soul to stop a Beast from being able to use Limb from Limb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:16:30-07:00","id":557237,"title":"","content":"Each atavism tells you what kind of action it takes to use. So yes, though I imagine some effects would remain even while &quot;off&quot;, specifically the extra Health from Looming Presene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:34:56-07:00","id":557453,"title":"","content":"Unbreakable and Wings of the Raptor have 'Persistent' as their action (for the normal affect), so I would say that they are always on, but any of the Reflexive ones can be turned off (or actually, not used) as desired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}